Feature: prune exclude-tag filter

  Rule: Exclude-tag preservation
    Done yaks carrying the excluded tag are kept; done yaks
    without it are still pruned.

    Example: Done yak with excluded tag is kept
      - "important" is done, tagged keep
      - prune --exclude-tag keep
      - "important" survives

    Example: Done yak without excluded tag is pruned
      - "old stuff" is done, no tags
      - prune --exclude-tag keep
      - "old stuff" is removed

    Example: Done yak with a different tag is pruned
      - "other" is done, tagged urgent
      - prune --exclude-tag keep
      - "other" is removed

  Rule: No flag means current behaviour
    Without --exclude-tag, all done yaks are pruned as before,
    even if they carry tags.

    Example: Tagged done yak pruned when no flag given
      - "important" is done, tagged keep
      - prune (no flag)
      - "important" is removed

  Rule: Excluded descendants preserve ancestors
    The iterative leaf-pruning algorithm means: if a tagged
    child is kept, its parent never becomes a leaf and is
    naturally preserved.

    Example: Excluded parent with done untagged child
      - parent "epic" is done, tagged keep
      - child "subtask" is done, no tags
      - prune --exclude-tag keep
      - "subtask" pruned, "epic" kept

    Example: Untagged done parent with excluded child
      - parent "wrapper" is done, no tags
      - child "important" is done, tagged keep
      - prune --exclude-tag keep
      - both kept (parent never becomes a leaf)
